add(18,[18,19],'idea of the earlier run',16,[41],[1586,1613],
'“L• bounded above, M• bounded below”',
'Off-topic reused RHom proposition: coherence follows for coherent complexes with L bounded above and M bounded below, or with both bounded below and a uniform Ext-vanishing hypothesis. Both bounded below alone is insufficient: over a field, complexes k in every nonnegative degree have H⁰RHom=∏_{n≥0}k.',
'The infinite-product counterexample is the earlier run’s test and is rechecked here; it does not contradict the actual additional uniform-vanishing alternative on the page.',
'agrees','The two entries concern the theorem’s boundedness qualification and its counterexample and are merged.')
